Scenario math (illustrative)
- Baseline: net burn = $195k → runway ≈ 6.15 months.
- 15% expense cut: monthly expenses → $795k × 0.85 = $675.75k → new net burn = $675.75k − $600k = $75.75k → runway ≈ 15.8 months.
- 10% revenue lift (no expense change): revenue = $660k → net burn = $795k − $660k = $135k → runway ≈ 8.9 months.
- 20% revenue lift: revenue = $720k → net burn = $795k − $720k = $75k → runway ≈ 16 months.
- Combined (10% revenue lift + 10% expense cut): expenses = $715.5k, revenue = $660k → net burn = $55.5k → runway ≈ 21.6 months.
- Fundraising to reach 12 months at current burn: need 12 × $195k = $2.34M total cash → raise ≈ $1.14M (assuming no change to burn).

Takeaway: modest cost cuts or modest revenue improvements (or both) dramatically lengthen runway. A 10–15% improvement on either side is high impact.

Priority actions — immediate (0–30 days)
